  "title": "Unified title",
  "summary": "AnyBottle and DisParQ both focus on building interpretable vision models by reducing dependency on large concept vocabularies and using a frozen backbone with an unsupervised concept pool. They demonstrate that annotation-free models can achieve task-specific performance while maintaining interpretability.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "AnyBottle reduces concept annotations by using a single recipe to build compact, task-specific CBMs.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "DisParQ learns discrete spatially grounded concept representations from a frozen vision-only self-supervised backbone without language supervision.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Both models achieve higher concept consistency than language-aligned models, and their performance is validated across multiple datasets.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
